<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plymouth Sound</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Plymouth Sound is a deep bay on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a> at the mouths of the rivers Tamar and Plym, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devon">Devon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a>. It shelters the port of Plymouth and the naval base at Devonport. A breakwater across its entrance, completed in the 1840s, made it one of the main anchorages of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a>, and harbours on its shores were used for trade since prehistoric times.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/plymouth-sound.jpg" alt="Plymouth Sound" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Bodman · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plymouth_Sound_and_Breakwater.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
